SOVEREIGN ENTERPRISE — credits and provenance

The spine (canonical envelopes, the verify-before-parse gate, the order-independent materialiser with its role tree,
RGA text, the transparency-log vault, double-entry books, data leases and crypto-shredding, the node, the
deterministic simulator, the AI-native office cost kernel), the live company and the white paper are original to
this build and MIT licensed.

Standards implemented: Ed25519 (RFC 8032) via WebCrypto; SHA-256 (FIPS 180-4); Merkle transparency logs with
inclusion and consistency proofs (RFC 6962 / RFC 9162); RGA sequence CRDT (Roh et al., 2011); observed-remove sets
and last-writer-wins registers (Shapiro et al., 2011).

The design lens the estate builds in — entropy-guided regulation (the Guided Entropy Principle), weighted
information pruning (WIPER), behavioural entropy signatures (BES) and dual-map checking — is the work of
GARY W. FLOYD, Lumiea Systems Research Division (a subsidiary of ThunderStruck Services, LLC), New Caney, Texas.

The compression and codec lineage the estate builds on — Konomi — is Thomas Frumkin's.

External figures in the white paper are cited in data/basis.json with their sources: ONS, HMRC (gov.uk), The
Pensions Regulator, DESNZ, ECB, Salesforce, Microsoft, Anthropic, ElevenLabs, NVIDIA, LMSYS, Apple and the UK
retailers named there. The office in the white paper is modelled, not a client.
